  "sn35.52:1.1": "The root sense of <i lang='pi' translate='no'>upassaṭṭha</i> (“contaminated”) is something that has been poured upon, or on which something has been let loose (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/an5.192/en/sujato#8.2'>AN 5.192:8.2</a>). Cf. Bṛhadāraṇyaka Upaniṣad 1.3.6: “They contaminated (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>upāsṛjan</i>) those gods with evil”, the evil being “unfit” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>apratirūpaṁ</i>) sights, sounds, etc. ",
